  "worked_solution": "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{3x-2} & >15 \\\\ {e}^{3x-2} & <-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause a power of a positive number is always greater than $0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{e}^{3x-2}>0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality ${e}^{3x-2}<-15$ has no solutions.",
